  In the third part, you kept arguing that the initial "i" or "u" in ii and
uu is pronounced differently than they are in other diphthongs, but it
explicitly is EXACTLY the same (see chapter 3)  aionys is correct.  There
are NO exceptions. "ii" is NOT irregular.  They have palatal onglides.
 They are formed exactly the same in front of the same vowel as they are in
front of different vowels.

            --gejyspa



